# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json
# Rename this file to pr_<YOUR_PR_NUMBER>.prdoc when opening the PR (e.g. pr_12345.prdoc)

title: Remove collation protocol version 1 (V1) support

doc:
  - audience: Node Dev
    description: |
      Collation protocol V1 has been removed from the node. Only V2 and V3 are supported.

      - `CollationVersion` enum no longer includes V1; `CollationProtocols` and related types
        now have only V2 and V3 variants.
      - The legacy notification protocol `/polkadot/collation/1` and the request-response protocol
        `CollationFetchingV1` (/polkadot/req_collation/1) are no longer registered or handled.
      - Collator and validator protocol logic, network bridge TX/RX, and the collator protocol
        subsystem only handle V2 and V3. Validators reject peers that open V1 notification streams.
      - In the experimental collator protocol, `Advertisement` now always has a required
        `prospective_candidate` field (V1 allowed it to be missing).

      Downstream client or collator implementations that depend on collation V1 will need to
      use V2 or V3.
  - audience: Node Operator
    description: |
      This is a breaking network change. Nodes that only speak collation protocol V1 will no
      longer be able to connect to validators. 
      Ensure your collators are upgraded to one of the supported LTS releases.

crates:
  - name: polkadot-node-network-protocol
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-network-bridge
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-collator-protocol
    bump: major
  - name: polkadot-service
    bump: major
  - name: cumulus-relay-chain-minimal-node
    bump: major
